Based on spectrochemical series, ligands are arranged in increasing order of crystal field strength

\mathrm{CO}>\mathrm{NH}_3>\mathrm{C}_2 \mathrm{O}_4^{2-}>\mathrm{N}^{3-}

Among the following ligands, $\mathrm{CO}$ is the strongest ligand, while $\mathrm{N}^{3-}$ is the weakest ligand.

